title: LO Relations
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: lo_relations_timer <= 0
max-visits: 36
frequency: 300
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; lo_relations_timer += 7;
card-image: img/union3.jpg
tags: workers_movement
go-to: unionrelations; unionrelations2 if lo_relations < 50

@unionrelations


= **LO Relations**

We are institutionally {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Our party and the trade union confederation was born as twins, originally united in a single organisation. For practical reasons this unity was dissolved, nonetheless we still appoint two members to their central comittee, and they still appoint two to ours.">welded with LO</span>!}, giving us many opportunities to coordinate our strategy.

- @transfer_funds: Transfer funds.
- @promise_reform: Promise reform.
- @discuss_ok71: Discuss the strategy ahead of OK71.
- @discuss_next_election: Plan for the next election.
- @easy_discard


@transfer_funds
on-arrival: resources -= 1; lo_relations += 7
subtitle: -1 resources
unavailable-subtitle: -1 resources

The LO leadership appreciates this gesture, and promises to make it up to us.

@promise_reform



@discuss_ok71
view-if: year >= 1970 or year == 1971 and month >= 2

LO currently expects to win a fourth week of paid vacation in the next round of national negotiations.

- @discourage: Make them moderate their demands in order to lighten the pressure on the economy.
- @support_them: Indicate that we agree with their demands.
- @really_support_them: We promise to mobilize our membership and run a campaign in support of the negotiations.
- @encourage_more: Encourage them to up their demands and prepare for conflict.


